Rust dependency license texts are included in each native development archive
under licenses/<crate>-<version>/. The artifact manifest records the active
dependency names, versions, SPDX expressions and copied license files for that
target. Cargo.lock pins the dependency resolution.

Generate these notices together with the executable using:

  cargo +1.93.0 run --locked -p xtask -- native-development --target TARGET --out DIRECTORY

The builder fails when an active dependency lacks packaged license metadata or
license text. Dependencies differ by target and enabled features; notices from a
different target must not be substituted.

The old JavaScript ws implementation is no longer included. Its MIT notice did
not license the Agent project itself. No project license is inferred here; the
artifact record reports project_license_included and release_ready separately.
